---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/pages/privacy.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | LIT Bible"
  description="The LIT Bible app privacy policy. Your reading life is your own — we collect nothing personally identifiable, and everything you create stays on your device."
  canonical="https://litbible.net/privacy"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "Privacy Policy — LIT Bible",
      "url": "https://litbible.net/privacy",
      "dateModified": "2026-04-08",
      "description": "The LIT Bible app privacy policy. Your reading life is your own — we collect nothing personally identifiable, and everything you create stays on your device.",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@type": "WebSite",
        "name": "LIT Bible",
        "url": "https://litbible.net"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "LIT Bible",
        "url": "https://litbible.net"
      }
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="privacy-page" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">

    <header class="privacy-header">
      <div class="privacy-header__inner">
        <h1 id="privacy-title" class="privacy-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="privacy-effective">
          Effective date: <time datetime="2026-04-08">April 8, 2026</time>
        </p>
        <p class="privacy-lede">
          The LIT Bible app is built on a simple principle: your reading life is
          your own. This policy describes what data the app handles and how.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-body">

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-collect">
        <h2 id="privacy-collect">What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing personally identifiable. The app does not collect your name,
          email address, device identifiers, or any information that could
          identify you as an individual.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-on-device">
        <h2 id="privacy-on-device">What stays on your device</h2>
        <p>
          Everything you create in the app — highlights, notes, and your reading
          position — is stored locally on your device using a private database.
          This data never leaves your device and is not accessible to us.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your app preferences (such as your chosen text size and whether you
          have completed the welcome tour) are stored in your device's standard
          preferences storage and remain on your device.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-content-updates">
        <h2 id="privacy-content-updates">Content updates</h2>
        <p>
          The app may periodically check our servers at litbible.net for updates
          to the Bible translation text. During this check, your device contacts
          our server and downloads any changed content. No information about you,
          your device, or your reading activity is sent to us during this
          process. The check is limited to comparing file versions and
          downloading updated text — nothing more.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-spotlight">
        <h2 id="privacy-spotlight">Spotlight Search</h2>
        <p>
          The app makes portions of the Bible text available through your
          device's built-in Spotlight search. This indexing happens entirely on
          your device and is not transmitted to us or to Apple.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-widget">
        <h2 id="privacy-widget">The home screen widget</h2>
        <p>
          The LIT Bible widget displays lectionary readings and liturgical
          calendar information. All widget data is computed on your device from
          information bundled with the app. The widget makes no network
          requests.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-external-links">
        <h2 id="privacy-external-links">External links</h2>
        <p>The app includes links to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Donorbox</strong> (litbible.net's contribution page) —
            opened in an in-app browser. We do not track whether you visit this
            page or make a contribution.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Apple Podcasts</strong> — opened in the system browser or
            Podcasts app. We do not track whether you follow this link.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>CreativeCommons.org</strong> — opened in the system browser
            to display the full license text.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          When you follow these links, you are subject to those third parties'
          own privacy policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-sharing">
        <h2 id="privacy-sharing">Sharing</h2>
        <p>
          When you select text and choose Share, your device's standard share
          sheet opens. The selected passage text is passed to whatever app you
          choose to share it with. We do not log what you share, where you share
          it, or how often.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-third-party">
        <h2 id="privacy-third-party">Third-party software</h2>
        <p>The app is built using two third-party software libraries:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>GRDB</strong> — an open-source database library. It stores
            your data locally on your device and makes no network connections of
            its own.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Supabase SDK</strong> — a library that supports optional
            cloud backup features. This feature is not active in the current
            version of the app. The library is included in preparation for a
            future update; it makes no network connections and does not collect
            any data in the current version.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-children">
        <h2 id="privacy-children">Children</h2>
        <p>
          The app does not collect personal information from anyone, including
          children. It contains no advertising and no social features.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-changes">
        <h2 id="privacy-changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we update this policy in a way that is material to how your data is
          handled, we will note it in the app's Translation Updates section and
          update the effective date above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-contact">
        <h2 id="privacy-contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy can be directed to the LIT Bible team at
          <a href="/contact">litbible.net/contact</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
